# 43 2. Department of Defense, Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense (Environmental Quality)  indicated that environmental statement is satisfactory;
# 75 3. Department of Health, Education, and Welfare, Assistant
Secretary for Health and Scientific Affairs  felt that
human impacts portion of environmental statement gave inadequate
attention to potential public health hazards associated with\nuse of ORV;
# 76 4. Department of Transportation, Assistant Secretary for Environment and Urban Systems  indicated concern over noise emitted by ORV. Suggested that environmental statement include a statement on the need to develop appropriate noise standards;
#109 5. Environmental Protection Agency, Office of Federal Activities and indicated particular interest in adverse noise impacts of
ORV and the measures to be taken to protect the public from
noise levels. With regard to noise standards and criteria,
advised that EPA will be promulgating standards and regulations
for recreational vehicles under Section 6 of the Noise Control Act
of 1972, and that these standards will apply to the manufacture
of such vehicles, but will be based, among other things, on the
conditions of use of the vehicle. Further indicated that EPA
believes these standards will be of assistance to land managers\nin applying noise-level criteria for ORV use on Interior lands;
#108 6. Tennessee Valley Authority, Director of Environmental Research and Development  felt that environmental statement covered the considerations which are pertinent to the proposed policies and guidelines concerning ORV;
# 41 7. Federal Communications Commission, Chairman  indicated general agreement with the objectives of the environmental statement. Expressed concern that provisions be made so that common carriers and others who have wire, cable, or radio communications facilities on public lands have reasonable access to such facilities to the extent necessary for construction, operation, and maintenance for such facilities. 
8. Department of the Interior:
#77 (a) Bureau of Land Management  Director  felt that environmental statement should contain additional discussion of impacts of various types of ORV and their impacts on different types of terrain; also felt that statement should clarify status of all Interior lands prior to designation of ORV use;
#86 (b) Bureau of Reclamation, Acting Commissioner  indicated general concurrence relative to the adequacy of the subject environmental statement;
